diff --git a/doc/man/man1/sbatch.1 b/doc/man/man1/sbatch.1
index 6714d01..ff22b57 100644
--- a/doc/man/man1/sbatch.1
+++ b/doc/man/man1/sbatch.1
@@ -1351,6 +1351,32 @@ Must be enabled with \fBSchedulerParameters=het_batch_each\fR. Set it on the
 command line or in the first component's options; it applies to all components.
 .IP
 
+.TP
+\fB\-\-het\-join\fR=<\fIjob_id\fR>
+Submit an ordinary batch job that becomes a new component of the running
+heterogeneous job \fIjob_id\fR when it starts. That heterogeneous job must
+belong to the same user, have been submitted with \fB\-\-het\-batch\fR=\fIeach\fR
+and \fB\-\-het\-reserve\fR, and have a running component. The new job gets the
+lowest free job ID reserved by it, \fIjob_id+N\fR, waits in the queue and is
+scheduled alone like any other job (it never waits for the other components),
+and when it starts it is attached as component \fIjob_id+N\fR: \fBsqueue\fR
+shows it as \fIjob_id+N\fR and "\fIscancel job_id\fR" cancels it with the other
+components (also while it is pending). It runs its own batch script with
+\fBSLURM_HET_JOB_ID\fR and \fBSLURM_HET_JOB_OFFSET\fR set. If every component
+of the heterogeneous job ends before it starts, it is cancelled, also while it
+is held. Not allowed with \fB\-\-jobid\fR.
+.IP
+
+.TP
+\fB\-\-het\-reserve\fR=<\fIcount\fR>
+Heterogeneous jobs with \fB\-\-het\-batch\fR=\fIeach\fR only. Reserve job IDs
+\fIjob_id+0\fR to \fIjob_id+count\-1\fR for this heterogeneous job: its
+components take the first ones and jobs submitted later with
+\fB\-\-het\-join\fR take the others. No other job gets these IDs while the
+heterogeneous job's record exists, also across slurmctld restarts.
+\fIcount\fR must be at least the number of components and at most 1024.
+.IP
+
 .TP
 \fB\-H, \-\-hold\fR
 Specify the job is to be submitted in a held state (priority of zero).
